import lib/process.dl

function [the|] bounded wait test interpreter:
    execute:
        return "python" if the process platform is Windows, else "python3"

set command to a process command for the bounded wait test interpreter
add "-u" as an argument to command
add "-c" as an argument to command
add "import sys,time;sys.stderr.write('ready');sys.stderr.flush();time.sleep(0.2);sys.exit(7)" as an argument to command

launch command and set child to it
print whether child was launched as a line

wait up to 1000 milliseconds for process activity from child and set activity to it
print whether (activity succeeded) and (activity reports activity) as a line
read the available standard error of child and set error to it
print (error's contents) as a line

wait up to 10 milliseconds for child and set early to it
print whether early succeeded as a line
print whether early does not report completion as a line

wait up to 2000 milliseconds for child and set finished to it
print whether finished succeeded as a line
print whether finished reports completion as a line
print whether (finished's exit code = (7 as a 64 bit integer)) as a line

clean up child and set cleaned to it
print whether cleaned succeeded as a line
